WEBVTT

00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:06.731
A robot sets off across a room.

00:00:06.791 --> 00:00:11.598
For the first few seconds, nobody watching
can tell where it is going.

00:00:11.658 --> 00:00:16.394
And that is exactly when people hesitate,
or step into its path.

00:00:17.944 --> 00:00:20.273
The shortest route is safe.

00:00:20.333 --> 00:00:22.685
But it keeps everyone guessing.

00:00:25.835 --> 00:00:31.460
A legible route bends early, and pays
extra distance to make itself clear.

00:00:31.519 --> 00:00:34.912
But here, the clearest way to say where it
is going,

00:00:34.862 --> 00:00:37.412
is the way it is not allowed to go.

00:00:43.962 --> 00:00:47.329
Legible Motion Bench measures that trade.

00:00:47.389 --> 00:00:50.791
Clarity, against distance, against safety.

00:00:50.851 --> 00:00:54.334
No human raters. No AI judge.

00:00:54.394 --> 00:00:59.018
Every number is computed exactly, from the
path and the world.

00:01:02.969 --> 00:01:07.311
Give a planner more distance to spend, and
a frontier appears.

00:01:07.371 --> 00:01:12.129
With five percent extra, its clearest
route still crosses the zone.

00:01:12.189 --> 00:01:15.313
At ten percent, it buys its way out.

00:01:20.063 --> 00:01:24.001
Then the same question goes to three
language models.

00:01:24.061 --> 00:01:28.462
Two of them cut straight through the zone,
five times out of five.

00:01:28.523 --> 00:01:31.754
The third finds an option the others
missed.

00:01:31.814 --> 00:01:36.435
It slips just under the boundary, and
stays well inside its budget.

00:01:38.585 --> 00:01:41.418
Now change the budget in the prompt.

00:01:41.478 --> 00:01:45.973
Nearly double it, and one model's spending
does not move at all.

00:01:46.032 --> 00:01:48.603
Another's climbs at every step.

00:01:48.663 --> 00:01:51.847
For one model, the budget is a constraint.

00:01:51.907 --> 00:01:54.398
For the other two, it is text.

00:01:56.147 --> 00:01:58.639
And of a hundred and twenty answers,

00:01:58.589 --> 00:02:02.144
a hundred and sixteen called themselves
legible.

00:02:02.204 --> 00:02:06.094
Including all twenty five that were not
even feasible.

00:02:10.844 --> 00:02:14.273
One caution, which the project states
itself.

00:02:14.333 --> 00:02:17.722
Three models, one prompt, one temperature.

00:02:17.782 --> 00:02:19.950
A pilot, not a finding.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:23.043
Legible Motion Bench.

00:02:23.103 --> 00:02:26.081
What clarity costs, measured exactly.
